From a1110b6a545b5d3a93515b22164049c6d9301b7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite-Emulator Dev <dev@auralite-emu.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:48:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U3 update

USB U3: EHCI register file, USBCMD-only doorbell, control transfers.

Capability registers (CAPLENGTH=0 shared BAR map, HCIVERSION 2.00,
HCSPARAMS N_PORTS=1|PPC, HCCPARAMS), USBSTS (HCHALTED/PSS/ASS) with the
guest's halt handshake and HCRESET self-clear, USBCMD (RS/HCRESET/
PSE/ASE/IAAD/ITC), PORTSC (CCS gating attached&&PP&&!OWNER, CSC latched
on CCS change + W1C, PR->PED+PEC, LS J-state, OWNER release) -- and the
async schedule now runs on USBCMD writes only.  SETUP qTDs execute real
control transfers against a minimal device model (device/config/string
descriptors, SET_ADDRESS, SET_CONFIGURATION, GET_STATUS, GET_MAX_LUN,
BOT RESET).

Three window quirks are measured against the sample firmware's
hand-tested dance and the guest driver's 1/2/4-byte access shapes:

- the 8-byte capability-root slurp answers 0 until the first USBCMD
  write (firmware usb_ff uses the low dword as a scratch pointer; a
  HCIVERSION at +0x02 would triple-fault it -- measured), after which
  the offset answers USBCMD for its QWORD RMW dance;
- +0x04 is HCSPARAMS until the first USBCMD write, USBSTS after (the
  driver reads caps once at init, then starts the halt handshake);
- the schedule advances on the USBCMD doorbell and at a deterministic
  instruction cadence (cpu_devices_tick hook, every 256 instructions),
  so the guest's RAM-polling ehci_run_async completes without MMIO
  kicks; qTDs only execute while Active, so re-walks are idempotent.

Measured (8 new unit vectors, 14 -> 22; once-per-phase NC: restoring
the doorbell-on-every-write defect reddens 'ok doorbell usbcmd only',
RC=134): guest receipts move from 'HCI version 0.00, 0 ports' /
'controller did not halt' to 'HCI version 2.00, 1 ports, PPC=1,
64-bit=0, companions=0' + '1 high-speed device(s) ready', enumeration
reaches and passes '[msc] mass storage candidate: addr=1 VID=0x0525
PID=0xa4a5 bulk_in=0x81 bulk_out=0x02 maxpkt=512' on the QEMU-parity
'AURALUSB' stick (16384 sectors), READ(10) sector 0 sees the magic;
determinism pairs byte-identical (firmware stdout+stderr; kernel boot
logs, same sha256).  make test + make test-sanitize green.
